      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case of a 42-year-old airline captain grounded for obstructive coronary artery disease is reviewed. The investigation showed two selective lesions on one vessel. A bypass procedure was successful. Postoperative evaluation demonstrated an above-average physical performance without any symptoms. Adequate blood flow in the coronary bed and no heart muscle damage were also shown. The criteria for return to work are discussed."},
